<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Wimoweh (Karl Denver)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1961</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover of the Weavers' version, released just after the Tokens' record</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Lion Sleeps Tonight (the Hounds)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1967</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Lion Sleeps Tonight (Robert John)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1971</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Vimmersvej (Flemming Jørgensen and Bamses Venner)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1975</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new Danish words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Lion Sleeps Tonight (Tight Fit)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1982</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Lion King (Disney film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1994</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used in the film</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Lion King (stage musical)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1997</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used in the musical</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Vimmersvej (Flemming Jørgensen, with two of Linda's daughters)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2003</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new recording, its earnings sent to Linda's daughters</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Lion King (film, sung by Seth Rogen and Billy Eichner)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2019</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Black Is King (Beyoncé)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2020</span><span class="sg-chain-h">uses the original &quot;Mbube&quot;; made in part after learning of Linda's story</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><a href="/songs/mbube">Mbube (Solomon Linda and the Evening Birds)</a> <span class="sg-chain-y">1939</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the original; Linda's final improvised notes became the new tune</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Wimoweh (the Weavers)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1951</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the version the Tokens remade, chant kept</span></li></ul></section>
